From 6e6445321ec1560b857e0d22d6166fa36ce94aed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 21:21:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The hero stops lying about its own number, and starts talking
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

F-205 — the homepage hero published `26026+ Years in Toronto` in its server
HTML, and `262626+` once the count-up finished. CountUp rendered its value
three times: a hidden width sizer, the live value, and an .sr-only copy.
visibility:hidden and .sr-only hide text from a person. They do not remove it
from the document, so every crawler, answer engine and reader mode read the
concatenation — on the one site whose entire strategy is being quotable by
machines, and on its only trust stat. Verified on ecowoods.ca, not inferred.

  · CountUp now renders ONE text node. Width comes from `min-width` in `ch`
    against the final string plus tabular figures, and the initial state is the
    target rather than zero, so the server emits the real figure and a
    JavaScript-off visitor keeps it.
  · The hero stat no longer uses CountUp: one text node, derived from
    BUSINESS_NAP.foundedYear, static, and not part of the rotation.
  · verify-ui-contract.mjs check 5 fails the build on both halves of the
    pattern — a *sizer* class in JSX, and a -sizer CSS rule that hides itself.
    SwipeDeck's mobile-only sizer is the single recorded allowance (F-206).

HeroRotator — fifteen ways of saying the same true thing. The eyebrow and the
headline decode character by character out of their own alphabet; the body
lines cross-fade. HERO_VARIANTS[0] is server-rendered in full, so the HTML a
crawler reads is the canonical brand line and never a scrambled one. The decode
writes textContent through a ref, so no React render runs during it. Nothing is
duplicated in the DOM — the h1 names itself with aria-label. It pauses on
hover, on focus, on a hidden tab, on demand (WCAG 2.2.2), and prefers-reduced-
motion switches it off entirely. The CTA is passed in and never rotates.

Four of the fifteen submitted lines were changed, each recorded in the file:
"99.7% dust capture" (retired in F-165, banned by verify:facts), a crew tenure
figure that contradicts /team's own stated position, and two facts now
interpolated from BUSINESS_NAP so they cannot go stale or trip verify:claims.

Hover glow — every button and every card lays a halo of its own colour on the
surface around it. One shared three-stop box-shadow driven by a --glow custom
property each family sets to the token it is already painted with, so retinting
a component moves its halo with it. box-shadow rather than a pseudo-element
because these components are overflow:hidden and would clip a ::after.

All 40 guards green.
